{"Setting used codes to null leaves them in the array, preventing the same index from being reused but keeping array length. After using all 10 codes, the array becomes [null, null, ..., null] which still takes storage space. Should use splice to remove the code instead.": 0.12738735973834991, "Backup codes are stored while twoFactorEnabled is still false. If the user never completes the setup (never enters the TOTP code), the codes remain in the database but are inaccessible, creating orphaned data.": 0.39120855927467346, "Memory leak potential - if the user reopens the modal multiple times during setup, previous blob URLs are not revoked until a new one is created. The URL should be revoked in cleanup (e.g., in resetState or useEffect cleanup).": 0.2960699498653412, "Missing tests for logging in with backup codes to ensure the primary feature works end-to-end.": 0.23865154385566711}